{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Init.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Init.Omega"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.chirality_split_from_reconstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.chirality_split_from_reconstruction","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L143-L147","doc":"`S⁺(0)` carries the DT constant `4`; `S⁻(0)` carries `3`; they differ, so the\n`5₂` datum is a genuine two-element chirality-split spectrum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.splus_unipotent_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.splus_unipotent_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L133-L136","doc":"The reconstructed determinant data: both leading Stokes matrices are\nunimodular (they are products of elementary matrices). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.inversion_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.inversion_relation","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L127-L131","doc":"**Inversion relation at `q → 0`** (GGM eq (17)): `S⁺(0)ᵀ · S⁻(0) = 1`, proved\nfrom the *reconstructed* matrices. Two separately-built products satisfying an\nexact inverse relation is a strong consistency signal on the eq-(98) input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.minus_nine_is_derived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.minus_nine_is_derived","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L119-L123","doc":"**The `−9` is a product artifact, not a transcribed number**: it is\n`DT(3,1)·DT(1,2) + DT(3,2) = (−3)·4 + 3`. This is the entry a transcription\nerror would most likely corrupt, and it is an output of the reconstruction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.sminus_reconstructed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.sminus_reconstructed","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L114-L117","doc":"**The typed `S⁻(0)` is exactly the eq-(97) product of the eq-(98)\nconstants.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.splus_reconstructed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.splus_reconstructed","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L110-L112","doc":"**The typed `S⁺(0)` is exactly the eq-(96) product of the eq-(98)\nconstants.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.SminusTyped","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.SminusTyped","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L104-L108","doc":"ditto for `S⁻(0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.SplusTyped","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.SplusTyped","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L97-L102","doc":"The matrices as **typed** in `FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit` /\n`FiveTwoStokesMatrixIdentities` (reproduced here for the comparison). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.SminusRecon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.SminusRecon","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L94-L95","doc":"`S⁻(0)` **reconstructed** as the eq-(97) product `S_{σ₁σ₃}S_{σ₂σ₃}S_{σ₂σ₁}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.SplusRecon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.SplusRecon","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L91-L92","doc":"`S⁺(0)` **reconstructed** as the eq-(96) product `S_{σ₃σ₁}S_{σ₃σ₂}S_{σ₁σ₂}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.dt_spectrum_three_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.dt_spectrum_three_four","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L83-L87","doc":"**The off-diagonal DT spectrum is `{3, 4}`** (up to sign): the constants\nappearing in eq (98) are exactly `±3` and `±4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.elem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.elem","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L79-L81","doc":"The elementary Stokes factor `S_{σᵢσⱼ} = I + DT(i,j)·E_{ij}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.DT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.DT","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L72-L77","doc":"GGM eq (98): the matrix of Stokes constants (Donaldson–Thomas invariants) of\n`5₂`, whose `(i,j)` entry sits at the Borel singularity `ι_{i,j}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.one","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L67-L68","doc":"The identity matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.tr","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L64-L65","doc":"Transpose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.mul","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L61-L62","doc":"Matrix product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.M3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.StokesMatrixProvenance.M3","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/StokesMatrixProvenance.lean#L58-L59","doc":"`3×3` integer matrices as index functions (core only — no Mathlib needed). ","signatureChunk":0}]}